cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SemioABSA (DSAA), our diagnostic suite, or empirical findings in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SemioABSA: Aspect-Anchored Tensive Semiotics for Dimensional Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Open-science implementation and empirical validation of Aspect-Anchored Semiotic
  Decomposition (DSAA), bridging Claude Zilberberg's Tensive Semiotics and Silva's
  (2021, 2023) subjective quantifications with Large Language Models on SemEval-2026
  Task 3 (DimABSA). Solves zero-shot Arousal collapse and Tensive Scope Spillover
  without fine-tuning (RMSE_VA = 1.2926 global / 1.3033 official blind dev, p = 2.44e-19).
authors:
